<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Legal Notice (General) — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Code of Civil Procedure 1908 (Section 80 where applicable), Indian Contract Act 1872</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>No stamp paper required; Sent on Advocate's official letterhead with professional seal</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Not applicable; Must be served via Registered Post with Acknowledgment Due (RPAD) and Speed Post</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Not required; Signed and issued directly by an enrolled Advocate under instructions of the client</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Territorial jurisdiction of the court having authority over the place of contract / default</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>Notice period usually 15 days or 30 days before institution of civil suit</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Copy of Invoices / Agreements / Purchase Orders; Proof of Outstanding Payment or Breach of Terms; Bank Account Statement reflecting non-payment / dishonour; Correspondence records (Emails, WhatsApp chats, Letters)</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">LEGAL NOTICE (GENERAL)</div>
<div class="draft-body">FORMAL LEGAL NOTICE
(Issued under instructions of Client through Registered Post A.D. & Speed Post)

Date: ___/___/2026
From:
ADVOCATE _____________________________________________
Bar Council Enrollment No.: __________________________
Office Address: ______________________________________
______________________________________________________
Mobile: ____________________ | Email: ________________

TO:
______________________________________________________
______________________________________________________
______________________________________________________
(Hereinafter referred to as the "ADDRESSEE / RECIPIENT")

SUBJECT: LEGAL NOTICE FOR PAYMENT OF OUTSTANDING SUM OF RS. ____________/- ALONG WITH ACCRUED INTEREST @ 18% P.A. ARISING FROM BREACH OF CONTRACT.

Sir/Madam,

Under instructions from and on behalf of my client, __________________________________________________, residing at ____________________________________________________ (hereinafter referred to as "my Client"), I hereby serve upon you this formal Legal Notice as under:

1. That my Client is engaged in the lawful business/profession of _________________________________ having high commercial reputation and integrity.

2. That on or about ___/___/____, you, the Addressee, approached my Client and entered into a valid commercial transaction / contract / agreement for ______________________________________________________.

3. That relying upon your representations, my Client duly performed all reciprocal contractual obligations, supplied goods / rendered services, and raised valid Invoices bearing Nos. ________________________________ dated ___/___/____ for a total sum of Rs. ____________/- (Rupees _________________________________________ only).

4. That despite receipt and unconditional acceptance of the said goods/services without protest, you have failed, neglected, and refused to clear the outstanding balance of Rs. ____________/-, despite repeated personal reminders, phone calls, and email communications dated ___/___/____.

5. That your deliberate failure to discharge the legitimate liability constitutes willful breach of contract, unjust enrichment, and actionable civil wrong under the Indian Contract Act, 1872.

NOW THEREFORE, I, on behalf of my Client, hereby call upon you to pay the entire outstanding amount of Rs. ____________/- (Rupees _________________________________________ only) along with interest @ 18% per annum from the due date until realization, together with Rs. 5,000/- towards the cost of this legal notice, within 15 (FIFTEEN) DAYS of the receipt of this notice, failing which:

My Client has given me peremptory instructions to initiate appropriate Civil Proceedings for recovery of dues along with damages, and/or Criminal Proceedings before the competent Court of Law at your sole risk, cost, and consequences.

A copy of this Legal Notice is retained in my office for future legal reference.

Yours faithfully,

___________________________________________
ADVOCATE FOR CLIENT
Bar Council Reg. No.: ______________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>